@format 1
@id ui-event.6abfb3a1d1e496be
@title Crop edges — Reset clicked
@section I. UI
@area UI event
@tabs Edit
@event-ref cs|PPanels/PInspectorCropUi.cs|PInspectorResetBuild|pResetButton|Click|1
@entry input
@summary Reset all four Crop edges to zero and clear the Crop box without changing the other Edit transform settings.
@tag click
@tag PInspector
@alias owner = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PInspector

[input] Reset clicked <input>
- Receive the click event from the Crop Reset button @ owner.PInspectorResetBuild
> route

[route] Reset Crop edges <process>
- Set Left, Top, Right, and Bottom to zero under Crop-event suppression @ owner.PInspectorEdgesReset
- Publish a cleared Crop rectangle so the viewer hides its Crop box @ owner.PInspectorEdgesReset
- Refresh ratio notices, resulting resolution, and Crop-tool appearance @ owner.PInspectorEdgesReset
> output

[output] Crop edges reset <output>
= The four Crop edge values are zero and the full rotated source resolution is shown.
= Ratio, rotation, flips, Apply, and persistence settings are unchanged.
